@startuml state-diagram-sftp-connection
title SFTP Connection State Machine (NfsSftpFsProvider / NfsSyncingByteChannel)

[*] --> Disconnected : NfsSftpFsProvider created

state Disconnected {
    [*] --> AwaitingConfig
}

state Connected {
    [*] --> Idle
    Idle --> Reading    : read(ByteBuffer)\n[ChannelSftp.get()]
    Reading --> Idle    : bytes returned / EOF
    Idle --> Writing    : write(ByteBuffer)\n[buffer dirty = true]
    Writing --> Idle    : ByteBuffer consumed
    Idle --> Flushing   : close()\n[dirty == true]
    Flushing --> Idle   : NfsSftpFsIO.put() complete\n[dirty = false]
}

state ChannelOpen <<fork>>

Disconnected --> ChannelOpen  : open(NfsSftpConfig, path)\nNfsSftpFsIO.connect(config)
ChannelOpen --> Connected     : JSch session established\nNfsSyncingByteChannel created
ChannelOpen --> Error         : AuthException / IOException

Connected --> Disconnected    : close()\n[NfsSyncingByteChannel flushed]
Connected --> Error           : I/O failure during read/write

Error --> Disconnected        : reconnect attempt\nor user dismisses error dialog

Disconnected --> [*]  : NfsFileSystem.close()
Error --> [*]         : fatal error / app exit

note right of Connected
  NfsSyncingByteChannel:
    position field is long (overflow-safe)
    write() guards against buffer overflow
    flush on close() if dirty
end note

note left of Disconnected
  NfsSftpConfig holds:
    host, port, user,
    password (from env var)
end note
@enduml
